# Protocol rows = LiteRT-LM's own benchmark() entry point: prefill forced to exactly 1024 tokens with no prompt, decode 256, context 2048 (methodology/protocol-gemma4.md "The spec"); comparable with the model card's figures, never pooled with the task-prompt long-context-1024-gen256 rows.
# Entry points: Mac = yardstick run --litert-native-benchmark 1024x256 --context-tokens 2048 (scripts/bench_matrix_mac.sh); iPhone = the app's --litert-native-benchmark 1024x256 flag with --context-tokens 2048 (scripts/bench_matrix_iphone.sh). Both runners also pass --task short-chat, which yardstick and the app read before the native branch.
# One launch = N calls of benchmark() in one process (N = the row's runs=, else RUNS, default 4), call 1 cold; each call prints one YARDSTICK_NATIVE_OK line (Mac: appended to the row's .jsonl; iPhone: the console log), not a schema-v1 record; scripts/import_native_benchmark.py lifts the lines into JSON.
# This file's protocol rows are LiteRT-LM's. On the Mac, MLX and llama.cpp also have a forced-prefill entry (scripts/bench_matrix_mac.sh): MLX's row is in matrices/native-benchmark-1024x256-v1.cells, llama.cpp has no row. Core AI's rows are in matrices/dashboard-coreai-v1-mac.cells and dashboard-coreai-v1-ios.cells. On the iPhone only LiteRT-LM and Core AI have one (scripts/bench_matrix_iphone.sh). llama-bench is the Android counterpart (matrices/dashboard-protocol1024-v1-android.cells).
# Prepared 2026-10-06; same model set, catalog ids and cooldowns as matrices/dashboard-longctx1024-v1.cells; the anchor=1 rows are those of matrices/anchors.cells.
# 2026-10-19: the Mac and iPhone Qwen3 0.6B LiteRT-LM rows, the anchor=1 rows included, moved from the catalog id
# litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B (qwen3_0_6b_mixed_int4.litertlm; its template drops the user turn on LiteRT-LM
# v0.18.0, google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM#3688) to litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B/dynamic_wi4b32_afp32
# (Qwen3-0.6B_dynamic_wi4b32_afp32.litertlm: dynamic INT4, block-32 weights, FP32 act); the same day the iPhone rows
# moved on to litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B/dynamic_int8: that INT4 file fails on the iPhone's Metal GPU under v0.18.0.


# ---- mac ----
mac mlx-swift mlx-community/Qwen3-0.6B-4bit short-chat anchor=1 runs=3
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B/dynamic_wi4b32_afp32 short-chat anchor=1 runs=3
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B/dynamic_wi4b32_afp32 native-benchmark-1024x256 context-tokens=2048
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-1.7B native-benchmark-1024x256 context-tokens=2048
mac litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048
mac litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-4B native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048
mac litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E4B-it-litert-lm native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048

# ---- ios ----
ios mlx-swift mlx-community/Qwen3-0.6B-4bit short-chat anchor=1 runs=3
ios litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B/dynamic_int8 short-chat anchor=1 runs=3
ios litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B/dynamic_int8 native-benchmark-1024x256 context-tokens=2048
ios litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-1.7B native-benchmark-1024x256 context-tokens=2048
ios litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048
ios litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3-4B native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048
ios litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E4B-it-litert-lm native-benchmark-1024x256 cooldown=300 context-tokens=2048
